# What `gcloud builds submit` uploads as the build context for the Foundation
# service images (packaging/foundation/Dockerfile.*). Without this file gcloud
# derives the ignore set from .gitignore alone, which still uploaded ~3.1 GiB /
# 67k files — enough that a transient network blip aborts the resumable upload.
#
# The images build one Rust binary out of the workspace (`cargo build -p
# lait-<post|feed-notify|relay>`), so the context needs every workspace member's
# Cargo.toml + sources and the lockfile — and nothing else. We start from the
# git ignores (drops all `target/`, `node_modules/`, etc.) and additionally drop
# the large trees that are NOT cargo workspace members and no Rust build reads.
# Keep in sync with Cargo.toml [workspace].members: never exclude a member.
# (gitignore syntax: patterns only, no trailing inline comments.)
#!include:.gitignore

.git/

# astrolabe-web (src-tauri is outside the workspace) + deprecated Flutter (~2.8 GiB)
apps/
# the React viewer (TypeScript); its wasm/bundle are fetched at runtime, not built here
viewer/
# prose only
docs/
# BrightScript + card/pill/media assets; receivers/reference (Rust) stays
receivers/roku/
